<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel FELS net profit up 18.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Keppel FELS net profit up 18.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  54.36  vs  46.02</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)		     6.00  vs   6.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		 26.00  vs  22.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			   854.99  vs 654.21</p>
<p>    Investment income		  1.40  vs   0.53</p>
<p>    Other income/interest income  13.50  vs  20.38</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  10.27  vs  16.52</p>
<p>    Depreciation,amortisation     35.38  vs  30.37</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    37.08  vs  38.04</p>
<p>    Associates			  24.58  vs  17.95</p>
<p>    Tax				    7.05  vs   5.63</p>
<p>    Minorities			  (0.25) vs  (4.34)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   (1.48) vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - Keppel FELS Ltd is a unit of diversified maritime group Keppel Corp.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
</text>
